# Independent diagnostics of `data/train.csv`
All diagnostics use training data only. The sample period is `Ts = 0.2` s, as supplied in TASK.md. `omega = atan2(sin(phi_next-phi),cos(phi_next-phi))/Ts` rad/s. `speed = (dx*cos(phi+Ts*omega/2)+dy*sin(phi+Ts*omega/2))/Ts` m/s is signed midpoint-projected speed. `lateral` m/s is its orthogonal component. Fits use ordinary least squares (`numpy.linalg.lstsq`) unless stated otherwise, with no starting values or random seed. Errors are root mean square residuals on the stated rows, not rollout errors. All coefficient lists are ordered as the named design-matrix columns; coefficient units are target units divided by column units. Sample indices and counts are dimensionless. Phase indices denote elapsed samples since a command change.
Rows: 450 samples; 447 within-trajectory transitions; 90 command-change transitions (includes initial transitions).
Command ranges on all training rows: `v_f` [0.000034312, 0.298155603] m/s; `v_a` [-0.948147536, 0.941160627] rad/s.
On all transitions lateral RMS = 0.000877932158 m/s; speed median = 0.106803458 m/s.

